-Glovinsky1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glovinsky</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Quigley</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name><name><surname>Dunkelberger</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name></person-group><year>1991</year><article-title>Retinal ganglion cell loss is size dependent in experimental glaucoma.</article-title><source>Invest Ophthalmol Vis Sci</source><volume>32(3)</volume><fpage>484</fpage><lpage>491</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2001923</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003931-Glovinsky2"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glovinsky</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Quigley</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name><name><surname>Pease</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Foveal ganglion cell loss is size dependent in experimental glaucoma.</article-title><source>Invest Ophthalmol Vis Sci</source><volume>34(2)</volume><fpage>395</fpage><lpage>400</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8440594</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003931-Jakobs1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jakobs</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name><name><surname>Libby</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name><name><surname>Ben</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>John</surname><given-names>SW</given-names></name><name><surname>Masland</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Retinal ganglion cell degeneration is topological but not cell type specific in DBA/2J mice.</article-title><source>J Cell Biol</source><volume>171(2)</volume><fpage>313</fpage><lpage>325</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16247030</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.00