</person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>High sensitivity of human melatonin, alertness, thermoregulation, and heart rate to short wavelength light.</article-title><source>J Clin Endocrinol Metab</source><volume>90(3)</volume><fpage>1311</fpage><lpage>1316</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15585546</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003931-Hattar3"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hattar</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kumar</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Tong</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Tung</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Central projections of melanopsin-expressing retinal ganglion cells in the mouse.</article-title><source>J Comp Neurol</source><volume>497</volume><fpage>326</fpage><lpage>349</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16736474</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003931-Morin1"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Morin</surname><given-names>LP</given-names></name><name><surname>Blanchard</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Provencio</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Retinal ganglion cell projections to the hamster suprachiasmatic nucleus, intergeniculate leaflet, and visual midbrain: bifurcation and melanopsin immunoreactivity.</article-title><source>J Comp Neurol</source><volume>465(3)</volume><fpage>401</fpage><lpage>416</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12966564</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0003931-Panda2"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Panda</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Provencio</surname>